# Eaten Alive (CR 601.2b, 701.21a, 701.13a): "As an additional cost to cast this spell, sacrifice a creature or pay {3}{B}. Exile
# target creature or planeswalker." Bot1 has only Mox Jet's {B} for the spell and a Memnite, so the sacrifice is the way to pay.
# Bot2's Mox Ruby (a noncreature artifact) is no legal target and is refused with the mana there; its Ornithopter is exiled.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Memnite
Eaten Alive
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Ornithopter
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Eaten Alive.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
Bot1.Hand.Eaten Alive.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet
Bot1.Graveyard = Eaten Alive; Memnite
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
Exile = Ornithopter
